<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marciano returns eight weeks after intake and one week after the sick visit for stomach pain. He stopped naproxen that day and started omeprazole, and the burning has eased to an occasional twinge before breakfast. The Helicobacter pylori stool test collected at the sick visit was negative, and the HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening tests from the preventive visit were negative, with no immunity to hepatitis B, so the vaccine series continues. He finished six weeks of physical therapy this week and does his exercises every morning. His back pain averages about 3 out of 10, he has had no leg pain for three weeks, and the numbness on his foot has gone. He wears the thumb splint at night and for yard work, and the thumb aches less. He walks every day, swims three times a week and has started to jog slowly on the flat without back pain. His weight is down by 2.6 kg since intake. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Back pain</td><td>3 out of 10; Oswestry 18%</td></tr><tr><td>Thumb pain</td><td>3 out of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Stomach</td><td>Much better on omeprazole; Helicobacter pylori stool antigen negative</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>89.4 kg, from 92.0</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

